# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

`stands_down` (`crates/ai/src/candidates.rs`) counts an enemy unit only when that unit could attack the AI's unit on its controller's next turn. That means it is in Attack Position or has Deft in Defense Position, it passes `can_swing`, and the engine's `attack_restriction` lets it attack this unit, which also covers Dormant and Flying out of reach (R783002). Only then does it ask `kills_and_survives`, as it does today. New ruling R2021000 amends R1759000's definition of a stand-down. Its tests, named `r2021000_…`, sit next to the R1759000 tests: no stand-down against an enemy in Defense Position without Deft, a Frozen one, one with Can't attack, or a Dormant one; a stand-down against one with Deft in Defense Position; and for a Flying unit in Attack Position, only against Flying or Ranged enemies. No constant changes, and `kills_and_survives` stays as it is.

